  "language": "en",
  "text": "7.4 Hello, I'm Noora. Today, I'm going to tell you about the results of my survey. My questions were on the topic of eating meat. A lot of people in the past liked to eat meat. Is this still the same? Or do we want to eat more food that comes from plants? I think this is an interesting topic. There were three questions in my survey, and I asked people from different cultures, not only my culture. My first question was, how often do you eat meat? You can see here that 19% of people eat it every day, and 28% eat it three or four times a week. 39% eat it about once a week. 14% of people don't eat meat at all. In one survey I looked at, in the past, only 4% of people didn't eat meat. That means the number of people who don't eat meat is growing. My second question was, do you eat more or less meat than in the past? The answer really surprised me. 58% of people eat the same as they did one year ago. Only 13% eat more, but 29% eat less. I think that's a large number. For these people, eating meat has a lot of problems. They don't think it's healthy, and they don't want to hurt animals. My last question was, do you want to eat less meat? So when you look here, 22% of people say no. It's their favorite food. But 78% say yes. Many of these people want to add more fresh fruit and vegetables to their meals. But here is something that was interesting to me. 19% want to eat food that looks and feels like meat, but is really made of plants. So imagine a burger that tastes like a meat burger, but it's made of plants. That's what more people want. So my conclusion is, people are changing their opinions about meat. They enjoy it, but more and more of us don't feel happy about eating it. What do you think?",
